### 2. Dynamic `import()` (Node.js & Browser Compatible)
If you want to keep the module loading asynchronous or if you are targeting a broader environment, you can import the JSON file directly as an ES Module. This works in Node.js >= 18 (with strict versioning checks in earlier versions depending on flags) and modern browsers.

